A||||8||JR||How long did your 2.8 alternator last?||||1||
Z||000000||JR||04-15-2001||07:35 PM||||Just changed my original alternator out.  It lasted 120,000 miles (210,000 km)!  But, I feel for anyone of you who should have to change one.  It is a pain in the butt. Git it off the braket then tried to lift it up out of engine compartment.  No way, exhaust manifold in the way.  So went to the shop manual, says it has to come out the bottom.  So remove the right rear wheel, take off the wheel well splash guards, and oh my lord, have 16years of mud, road grime, and rust falling out.  Then the manual says to remove the tierod link from the hub and slide alternator out from behind the strut.  Spent half hour just trying to get the rusted corroded cotter bin off the nut holding the endlink to the balljoint, then tried to knock the balljoint off, no way in hell!!  So had to gently move the brake line located in front of strut and take out alternator.  Careful as these brake lines are now delicate with age and thus corrosion.  Good news--only took an hour to get it all back together.  HAPPY EASTER everyone.  That's how I spent my holiday weekend.  BTW alternator cost 120 $CDN (80$US)<P>------------------<BR>85GT (daily driver 120,000 miles)<BR>88GT (highly modified sunday driver)||||reg||1
Z||000001||grinthock||04-15-2001||08:02 PM||||The first one in my 85 lasted 40k, then the 2nd one is still gong strong 30K, but I have a stereo in that car that kills it, and no Cap.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||04-15-2001||08:14 PM||||OK. I feel slightly better about dropping $350 to have mine replaced (including towing). Since I don't really have tools or the place to do the work in our unpredictable weather, I'd say that sounds almost worth it. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||p4n1c||04-15-2001||08:16 PM||||12 years and 380,000kms.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Dad never replaced it and one day it just didn't work anymore.  Killed a battery that was in 5 years(he was told that was bad, they should be replaced every 3 or something like that).  The car had been running off the battery for about 5kms after the alternator died, then it died.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>He now makes sure to replace parts when they should be replaced.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||10
Z||000004||Fformula88||04-15-2001||08:20 PM||||Although my original is still going strong at 80K, I can feel your pain.  Last summer the bracket that holds it cracked and needed to be replaced.  Foolishly I figured it wouldn't take long.  I did find a good way to get the alternator out!  I removed the dogbone and the metal bracket that goes to the engine.  This gave me enough room to get the alternator out, but barely!  It was easier than taking the suspension apart!||||reg||1
Z||000005||GoCartGuy||04-15-2001||08:25 PM||||16 years and 152,000 miles.  Still got the stock one there and praying it stays in good shape.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||04-15-2001||10:00 PM||||My 87 still has the original.<P>The 88's got replaced in 98, it died while I was on the track at Daytona.  What a bummer.||||reg||1
Z||000007||PatrickB||04-16-2001||12:01 AM||||Mine lasted 170,000 miles before it started acting all funky on me.  <P>On the side, dont listen to haynes about changing the alternator and then you dont have to remove anything but the alternator  and passenger tire.<P>If Im in a good working mood I can change one  in about 30 minutes for the GT.<P>Pat||||reg||14
Z||000008||Standard||04-16-2001||12:13 AM||||I'm pretty sure mine was original when it died at the 154,000 mile mark.  Sure looked original...||||reg||1
